/* War Room 13.26 · capmap.js — THE CAPABILITY MAP (B3) and the real-world evidence loop (B4).
   Not a second academy. It sits on top of the existing Bootcamp:
     · ideas, lessons and the six-stage ladder stay in bootcamp.js (bcRung) and capability.js (cpDims);
     · this file groups the existing cards into capabilities across nine domains, says what competence looks like,
       and keeps KNOWLEDGE (the ladder of the mapped ideas) apart from PERFORMANCE (real events, judged with evidence).
   A capability with no mapped card is listed as MISSING CONTENT. Nothing is invented to fill it.
   Performance evidence lives in S.boot as cx:<capId> = { log: [{ at, eff, out, comp, ev, note, src, ctx }] }.
     eff  = effort    : did / part / avoided       (did I actually try it)
     out  = outcome   : good / mixed / bad         (what happened, which luck also decides)
     comp = competence: yes / part / no            (did I perform the skill to standard)
   Only comp 'yes' WITH written evidence counts as demonstrated. A logged call, a logged event, an outcome on its own,
   a simulation or a high confidence never counts. Levels: 0 none · 1 attempted · 2 partly · 3 demonstrated ·
   4 reliable (3+ demonstrations on 3+ days) · 5 transferred (demonstrated in 2+ different contexts). */
